"8fb55e182fa8a1f37a7b":{"version":"Text considered: Christ Arose. Published hymn transcription; the exact stanza selection and recording remain for human verification. This report concerns the catalog text, independently of personal or imported assessments.","summary":"A preliminary AI reading of doctrinal accuracy, theological substance, and language, with separate catalog text scores. The reasons explain these provisional scores, not your personal or imported judgments. No church-use decision is made.","reasons":[{"criterion":"Doctrinal accuracy","explanation":"Jesus' resurrection is presented as real victory over death and the grave, followed by enduring life and reign with his people. Human guards and seals cannot prevent divine victory."},{"criterion":"Theological substance","explanation":"Burial, failed attempts to secure the tomb, death's defeat and lasting reign give the refrain several supports. The text focuses on resurrection rather than explaining the cross's saving mechanism."},{"criterion":"Language & craftsmanship","explanation":"The contrast between quiet burial verses and triumphant refrain is inherent in the words. Describing death as a defeated captor is recognizable personification rather than a separate account of events beneath the grave."}],"scores":{"accuracy":9,"substance":8,"language":8,"time":null},"quote":"","concerns":[],"themes":["Resurrection","Victory over death","Reign of Christ"],"scriptures":[{"reference":"Matthew 28:6","quote":"He is not here: for he is risen, as he said. Come, see the place where the Lord lay.","relationship":"Supporting comparison","explanation":"Compare the passage in context with the lyric's treatment of resurrection, victory over death, reign of christ. This is a comparison for review, not a claim that the writer intended a verbal quotation.","translation":"KJV"},{"reference":"Acts 2:24","quote":"Whom God hath raised up, having loosed the pains of death: because it was not possible that he should be holden of it.","relationship":"Supporting comparison","explanation":"Compare the passage in context with the lyric's treatment of resurrection, victory over death, reign of christ. This is a comparison for review, not a claim that the writer intended a verbal quotation.","translation":"KJV"},{"reference":"Romans 6:9","quote":"Knowing that Christ being raised from the dead dieth no more; death hath no more dominion over him.","relationship":"Supporting comparison","explanation":"Compare the passage in context with the lyric's treatment of resurrection, victory over death, reign of christ. This is a comparison for review, not a claim that the writer intended a verbal quotation.","translation":"KJV"}],"source":{"url":"https://github.com/ChurchApps/WorshipCommonsContent/blob/d3362e1d7c7f4d3f98b9310bb07aa480453508c7/songs/en/christ-arose-SfCJUXo-bOS/sources/lyrics.chordpro","label":"Christ Arose · Robert Lowry · source transcription","kind":"published-hymnal","checkedAt":"2026-10-17","hash":"c63fccb86eacfe96ffd9b7255e9f8a1a429204367a2ae35a7ebb14099dd291e6"},"limits":["The supplied transcription may omit, alter or misattribute a stanza. Compare it with your selected text before using the assessment.","Artist association does not verify a specific recording. No tempo, key, duration, arrangement or instrumental quality was inferred.","Human judgments, saved concerns, personal themes, recordings, approvals, libraries and plans are unchanged.","A supporting Scripture comparison is distinct from a verified quotation or deliberate allusion in the song."]},
