"f8bf645b93133a38e2bd":{"version":"Text considered: Alas! and Did My Savior Bleed. Published hymn transcription; the exact stanza selection and recording remain for human verification. This report concerns the catalog text, independently of personal or imported assessments.","summary":"A preliminary AI reading of doctrinal accuracy, theological substance, and language, with separate catalog text scores. The reasons explain these provisional scores, not your personal or imported judgments. No church-use decision is made.","reasons":[{"criterion":"Doctrinal accuracy","explanation":"The Savior's suffering is connected with the singer's guilt and undeserved grace, while tears are expressly denied the power to repay saving love. Self-giving is a grateful response rather than a substitute ransom."},{"criterion":"Theological substance","explanation":"The selected five stanzas move through Christ's death, personal sin, creation's darkness, thankful sorrow and the surrender of life. Redemption has both an objective saving basis and a developed personal response."},{"criterion":"Language & craftsmanship","explanation":"Repeated questions make the wonder concrete, and the final contrast between unpayable love and a life offered in thanks resolves the argument. The Maker's death refers to Christ's genuine human death, not the end of God's existence."}],"scores":{"accuracy":9,"substance":8,"language":9,"time":null},"quote":"","concerns":[],"themes":["Atonement","Grace","Repentance","Surrender"],"scriptures":[{"reference":"Isaiah 53:5","quote":"But he was wounded for our transgressions, he was bruised for our iniquities: the chastisement of our peace was upon him; and with his stripes we are healed.","relationship":"Supporting comparison","explanation":"Compare the passage in context with the lyric's treatment of atonement, grace, repentance, surrender. This is a comparison for review, not a claim that the writer intended a verbal quotation.","translation":"KJV"},{"reference":"Romans 5:8","quote":"But God commendeth his love toward us, in that, while we were yet sinners, Christ died for us.","relationship":"Supporting comparison","explanation":"Compare the passage in context with the lyric's treatment of atonement, grace, repentance, surrender. This is a comparison for review, not a claim that the writer intended a verbal quotation.","translation":"KJV"},{"reference":"Romans 12:1","quote":"I beseech you therefore, brethren, by the mercies of God, that ye present your bodies a living sacrifice, holy, acceptable unto God, which is your reasonable service.","relationship":"Supporting comparison","explanation":"Compare the passage in context with the lyric's treatment of atonement, grace, repentance, surrender. This is a comparison for review, not a claim that the writer intended a verbal quotation.","translation":"KJV"}],"source":{"url":"https://hymnary.org/text/alas_and_did_my_savior_bleed","label":"Alas! and Did My Savior Bleed · Representative hymn text · source transcription","kind":"published-hymnal","checkedAt":"2026-10-18","hash":"d9e55e3ea44021c72f9da32cb8d35ab797972a1169adb9ab0c20a1feb82142b7"},"limits":["The supplied transcription may omit, alter or misattribute a stanza. Compare it with your selected text before using the assessment.","Artist association does not verify a specific recording. No tempo, key, duration, arrangement or instrumental quality was inferred.","Human judgments, saved concerns, personal themes, recordings, approvals, libraries and plans are unchanged.","A supporting Scripture comparison is distinct from a verified quotation or deliberate allusion in the song."]},
